ntry_window of each other; the other vehicle bears to the subject's right in the subject's frame, so that the subject is the vehicle on the left. The duty does not apply where an official traffic-control device governs that junction or the subject's approach carrier -- unless either node of subsection 4 is engaged for the subject at that junction, which suspends that exception -- and it does not apply where the two carriers' designated directions are opposed and either vehicle is declared to intend a left turn at that junction or is making one.", "obligation": "From the entries on, the subject must grant precedence to the vehicle on its right: it must not enter the junction at an observation at which that vehicle lies within it, must not come into contact with it, and must not let its closest approach to it under constant velocities within p.yield_conflict_horizon fall below p.yield_min_clearance while that vehicle is within the junction.", "params": ["p.simultaneous_entry_window", "p.same_direction_cosine_tolerance", "p.heading_since_step_carla_scene_graph", "p.turn_onset_yaw_rate", "p.left_turn_angle", "p.yield_conflict_horizon", "p.yield_min_clearance"], "narrowings": [{"span": "ob1", "why": "'shall yield the right-of-way' is read as granting precedence in the three observable ways the definition's 'danger of a crash unless one grants precedence' admits on a trace: no entry while the right-hand vehicle lies within the junction, no contact, and no closest approach within the horizon closer than the clearance. Where both vehicles are already within the junction the first of the three is spent and the other two carry the duty.", "kind": "reading"}, {"span": "s1", "why": "'the driver of the vehicle on the left' is read through the vehicle's controlled motion: who or what is at the controls is not observable, and the duty binds that vehicle's conduct.", "kind": "observable_reading", "category": "agency"}, {"span": "e1", "why": "'official' is read as the presence of the device on the road: the feature's presence is the observable evidence of its official status.", "kind": "observable_reading", "category": "status"}], "scenarios": [{"name": "forbid", "expected": "violated", "narrative": "An unsignalised, unsigned crossing of two highways. A car and a van enter the junction within half a second of each other, each from a lane lying on a different highway, and the van bears to the car's right. The car keeps its speed, closes on the van inside the junction and the two bodies touch.", "masked": []}, {"name": "permit", "expected": "compliant", "narrative": "The same crossing and the same two entries within half a second, the van again on the car's right. The car brakes immediately inside the junction, stays well clear of the van throughout and lets it pass: no contact and no closest approach within the horizon below the clearance bound.", "masked": []}, {"name": "idle", "expected": "not_applicable", "narrative": "The car and the van enter the same junction from different highways, but eight seconds apart: the entries are not within the simultaneity window, so the rule is not engaged.", "masked": []}, {"name": "blind", "expected": "unknown", "narrative": "Both vehicles enter the junction within half a second from different highways, but the source does not report the direction of the van from the car in the car's frame, so which vehicle is on the left is unknown and the rule reports unknown.", "masked": ["rel.bearing"]}, {"name": "branch_1", "expected": "not_applicable", "narrative": "The two vehicles enter the same junction simultaneously from different highways, but a traffic signal governs the junction and is operating normally: the section does not apply at a junction controlled by an official traffic-control device and no node of subsection 4 is engaged.", "masked": []}, {"name": "branch_2", "expected": "violated", "narrative": "The same signalised junction with its heads installed, uncovered and dark, so subsection 4 is engaged for the car and the device exception is suspended. The car and the van enter simultaneously from different highways, the van on the car's right, and the car drives into it.", "masked": []}, {"name": "branch_3", "expected": "not_applicable", "narrative": "A car on the left and a van on its right enter a junction simultaneously, but the two carriers they enter by have opposed designated directions and the source declares the car's current plan to be a left turn at that junction: the section does not apply.", "masked": []}], "literals": [], "param_proposals": [{"name": "p.same_direction_cosine_tolerance", "unit": "ratio", "value": 0.866, "convention": "Heading-agreement convention: the cosine of the largest angle between two directions still read as the same direction, set at thirty degrees; its negative is the bound at which two directions are read as opposed.", "source": "The thirty-degree sector convention used for same-direction and opposed-direction tests in traffic conflict analysis."}, {"name": "p.turn_onset_yaw_rate", "unit": "deg/s", "value": 3.0, "convention": "Manoeuvre-onset convention: the rate of change of heading above which a body is read as turning rather than running straight, set above the yaw noise of a vehicle holding its lane.", "source": "Yaw-rate channel noise and lane-keeping figures from instrumented-vehicle studies."}, {"name": "p.left_turn_angle", "unit": "deg", "value": 45.0, "convention": "Turn-recognition convention: the heading change accumulated since the onset at which a turn to the left is recognized as made, rather than as a lane change or a bend taken.", "source": "Manoeuvre-recognition practice: half the ninety-degree heading change of a right-angle junction turn."}, {"name": "p.yield_conflict_horizon", "unit": "s", "value": 3.0, "convention": "Conflict-avoidance convention: the time ahead of the observation over which a closest approach under constant velocities is read as the 'danger of a crash' the right-of-way definition names, rather than as a passing of two road users on diverging paths.", "source": "Surrogate-safety practice for time-to-conflict measures at junctions (post-encroachment and time-to-collision thresholds of two to three seconds)."}, {"name": "p.yield_min_clearance", "unit": "m", "value": 2.0, "convention": "Conflict-avoidance convention: the clearance between the nearest points of two bodies below which a closest approach is read as a failure to grant precedence rather than as a safe passing.", "source": "Lateral and longitudinal clearance practice for passing a road user at low speed in a junction."}, {"name": "p.simultaneous_entry_window", "unit": "s", "value": 1.0, "convention": "Arrival-simultaneity convention: the interval between two vehicles' entries into one junction within which the two are still both inside the junction's conflict area at ordinary approach speeds, so that their entries count as at approximately the same time; taken as the time a vehicle needs to clear the conflict area of a small urban junction at a crossing speed.", "source": "Gap-acceptance and conflict-area clearance practice for unsignalised junctions (critical gap and follow-up headway tables of the Highway Capacity Manual)."}], "gaps": []}
{"node_id": "NRS_484B_253_o1", "law_refs": ["NRS-484B-253"], "subject": {"binder": "v", "class_elements": ["ru.aggregate=DEF-NRS-484A-320::vehicle"]}, "segmentation": [{"id": "s1", "text": "The driver of a vehicle", "role": "subject"}, {"id": "t1", "text": "within an intersection", "role": "trigger"}, {"id": "c1", "text": "intending to turn to the left", "role": "condition"}, {"id": "ob1", "text": "shall yield the right-of-way to any vehicle approaching from the opposite direction which is within the intersection", "role": "obligation"}, {"id": "st1", "text": "or so close thereto as to constitute an immediate hazard,", "role": "standard"}, {"id": "sib1", "text": "but such driver, having so yielded and having given a signal when and as required, may make such left turn and the drivers of all other vehicles approaching the intersection from the opposite direction shall yield the right-of-way to the vehicle making the left turn.", "role": "sibling"}], "elements": [{"span": "s1", "atoms": ["ru.aggregate=DEF-NRS-484A-320::vehicle"], "derived": [], "justification": "'The driver of a vehicle' binds the subject: DEF-NRS-484A-080 makes the driver the person who drives or is in actual physical control of the vehicle, and the ontology reads 'the driver' through the vehicle's controlled motion, so the duty binds that vehicle. Its class is the admitted aggregate ru.aggregate=DEF-NRS-484A-320::vehicle, claimed as one atom and never expanded into the classes it covers; the mapping index maps the same words to the same atom."}, {"span": "t1", "atoms": ["rel.occupies", "st.intersection"], "derived": [], "justification": "'within an intersection' is rel.occupies, 'a road user's footprint overlaps a lane / region (roadway, shoulder, sidewalk, intersection, ...)', on a region of kind st.intersection, 'the region where two roadways meet, bounded by the prolongation of their edges'. rel.occupies is the anchor that makes the junction the subject's own and the kind-ranging relation the region quantifier needs; st.intersection is not a stand-in for a crosswalk or a stop line, and none is read here. The junction this element binds is the one every later condition of this node reads, the intention's target included."}, {"span": "ob1", "atoms": ["ru.aggregate=DEF-NRS-484A-320::vehicle", "rel.occupies", "st.intersection", "st.travel_region", "st.lane_enters", "st.lane_direction", "rel.surface_gap", "rel.contact", "kin.speed", "prim.closest_approach_within", "prim.closest_approach_distance"], "derived": [], "justification": "'any vehicle' is the term DEF-NRS-484A-320 defines, the admitted aggregate ru.aggregate=DEF-NRS-484A-320::vehicle, claimed as one atom for the road users quantified over inside the obligation. 'approaching from the opposite direction' is read as the ontology directs, since rel.oncoming is 'not a stand-in for the direction a road user approaches from -- that is read through the carrier it approaches through, any carrier st.lane_enters admits ..., whose entrance end is the intersection, and through that carrier's direction (st.lane_direction) at the same instant': the other vehicle occupies (rel.occupies) a carrier of kind st.travel_region whose entrance end is the junction t1 binds (st.lane_enters), and that carrier's designated direction is opposed to the direction of the carrier by which the subject came to the junction, their normalised dot product lying at or below the negative of p.same_direction_cosine_tolerance. This reading is what the words need here, because the subject's own heading swings through the turn while the direction it approached from does not change. 'which is within the intersection' is rel.occupies on the same st.intersection region. 'shall yield the right-of-way' is DEF-NRS-484A-210's right 'to proceed in a lawful manner in preference to another vehicle ... unless one grants precedence to the other': the subject grants precedence by not coming into contact with that vehicle (rel.contact, 'the bodies of two road users ... touch or overlap') and by not letting its closest approach to it fall below the clearance, which prim.closest_approach_within and prim.closest_approach_distance give under constant velocities within the horizon and rel.surface_gap measures between the nearest points of the two bodies, with kin.speed the subject's own speed. rel.surface_gap is not read as an order of arrival; rel.contact is not a stand-in for a near miss, which is why the primitives stand beside it."}], "operationalizations": [{"span": "st1", "standard": "or so close thereto as to constitute an immediate hazard", "concepts": ["st.region_geometry", "st.intersection", "kin.speed", "rel.surface_gap", "prim.closest_approach_within", "prim.closest_approach_distance"], "params": ["p.yield_headway_time", "p.yield_conflict_horizon", "p.yield_min_clearance"], "convention": "Gap-acceptance convention for a left turn across an opposing stream. 'So close thereto' is the oncoming vehicle's distance to the junction, which st.region_geometry gives as 'the ground distance from a road user's body outline to it'; the hazard is read by the degree to which the words hold, the distance divided by nothing but carried as a product -- the vehicle is so close where that distance is at most its own speed (kin.speed) times p.yield_headway_time, so a faster approach makes a greater distance count and a slower one a smaller. The immediacy of the hazard is read in the same breath by the conflict-avoidance convention: the closest approach between the two bodies under constant velocities within p.yield_conflict_horizon falling below p.yield_min_clearance, measured between the nearest points of the bodies by rel.surface_gap. Both bounds are the reading's, set from gap-acceptance tables for a permitted left turn, and neither is a figure of the law's.", "surrogate": false}], "assumptions": [], "intentions": [{"span": "c1", "id": "int.left_turn", "meaning": "the source's current plan for the road user is that it turn to the left at the region named as the declaration's target"}], "compositions": [], "residues": [], "binders": [{"name": "v", "class_elements": ["ru.aggregate=DEF-NRS-484A-320::vehicle"]}], "applicability": "The subject vehicle's footprint overlaps an intersection and the source declares its current plan to be a left turn at that intersection. The declaration is read at the judged observation or earlier, never ahead of it, and the act of turning is not what engages the rule: an intention the plan still holds engages it even while the vehicle waits.", "obligation": "At every such observation the subject must grant precedence to every vehicle of the aggregate that occupies a carrier whose entrance end is that intersection and whose designated direction is opposed to the direction of the subject's own approach carrier, and that either lies within the intersection or is so close to it as to constitute an immediate hazard -- its distance to the junction region at most its speed times p.yield_headway_time, or its closest approach to the subject under constant velocities within p.yield_conflict_horizon below p.yield_min_clearance. Granting precedence is: no contact with that vehicle, and no closest approach to it within p.yield_conflict_horizon below p.yield_min_clearance.", "params": ["p.same_direction_cosine_tolerance", "p.yield_headway_time", "p.yield_conflict_horizon", "p.yield_min_clearance"], "narrowings": [{"span": "ob1", "why": "'shall yield the right-of-way' is read as granting precedence in the two observable ways open to a vehicle already within the junction: no contact with the oncoming vehicle, and no closest approach within the horizon closer than the clearance. A deference that shows in neither is outside what a trace can check; the duty is not read as a prohibition on turning at all, which the words do not state.", "kind": "reading"}, {"span": "ob1", "why": "'approaching from the opposite direction' is read through the designated direction of the carrier by which e