{"name": "p.yield_min_clearance", "unit": "m", "value": 2.0, "convention": "Conflict-avoidance convention: the clearance between the nearest points of two bodies below which a closest approach is read as a failure to grant precedence rather than as a safe passing.", "source": "Lateral and longitudinal clearance practice for passing a road user at low speed in a junction."}], "gaps": []}
{"node_id": "NRS_484B_253_o2", "law_refs": ["NRS-484B-253"], "subject": {"binder": "v", "class_elements": ["ru.aggregate=DEF-NRS-484A-320::vehicle"]}, "segmentation": [{"id": "sib1", "text": "The driver of a vehicle within an intersection intending to turn to the left shall yield the right-of-way to any vehicle approaching from the opposite direction which is within the intersection or so close thereto as to constitute an immediate hazard,", "role": "sibling"}, {"id": "c1", "text": "but such driver, having so yielded", "role": "condition"}, {"id": "c2", "text": "and having given a signal when and as required,", "role": "condition"}, {"id": "c3", "text": "may make such left turn", "role": "condition"}, {"id": "s1", "text": "and the drivers of all other vehicles approaching the intersection from the opposite direction", "role": "subject"}, {"id": "ob1", "text": "shall yield the right-of-way to the vehicle making the left turn.", "role": "obligation"}], "elements": [{"span": "c2", "atoms": ["sig.turn_indicator", "sig.hand_signal"], "derived": [], "justification": "'having given a signal' is the signal the left-turning vehicle emits: sig.turn_indicator, whose 'state is off, left or right: neither indicator lit, or the left or the right one', shown as left, or sig.hand_signal, 'a driver's or rider's arm signal; meaning is no_signal, left, right, stop_or_slow, re_enter', given as left. sig.turn_indicator is 'not a stand-in for the turn or lane change itself', and it is not used for one here: the turn is carried separately by its own concept in c3, and this span carries only the indication. 'when and as required' is read through the signalling convention: a left indication at some observation in the window p.turn_signal_advance_window behind the turn's recognition. The condition is read on the left-turning vehicle the obligation quantifies over, not on the subject."}, {"span": "c3", "atoms": ["rel.occupies", "st.intersection"], "derived": ["drv.motion.left_turn"], "justification": "'may make such left turn' names the manoeuvre drv.motion.left_turn denotes, 'the road user has turned to the left: counting from the onset of the turning ... the heading change accumulated since that onset reaches at least the turn angle ... to the left', read on the left-turning vehicle while its footprint overlaps the junction: rel.occupies ('a road user's footprint overlaps a lane / region') on a region of kind st.intersection ties the turn to the junction the subject approaches, so that a left turn made elsewhere in the scene does not raise this duty. The concept states the turning of the body only, and neither a signal nor a declared intention stands in for it."}, {"span": "s1", "atoms": ["ru.aggregate=DEF-NRS-484A-320::vehicle", "rel.occupies", "st.travel_region", "st.lane_enters", "st.lane_direction", "st.intersection"], "derived": [], "justification": "'the drivers of all other vehicles' binds the subject: the driver is read through the vehicle's controlled motion, so the subject is each other vehicle of the admitted aggregate ru.aggregate=DEF-NRS-484A-320::vehicle, claimed as one atom. 'approaching the intersection' is the ontology's own reading, 'a carrier it occupies (rel.occupies) whose entrance end is that intersection (st.lane_enters)', with st.travel_region the kind that carrier quantifier ranges over and st.intersection the junction at which the left turn is made. 'from the opposite direction' is read, as the ontology directs for these words, through that carrier's designated direction st.lane_direction being opposed to the direction of the carrier by which the left-turning vehicle reached the junction, their normalised dot product at or below the negative of p.same_direction_cosine_tolerance; rel.oncoming is expressly not a stand-in for the direction a road user approaches from, and the left-turning vehicle's heading swings through its turn, so the carriers and not the headings are read."}, {"span": "ob1", "atoms": ["ru.aggregate=DEF-NRS-484A-320::vehicle", "rel.occupies", "st.intersection", "rel.surface_gap", "rel.contact", "kin.speed", "prim.closest_approach_within", "prim.closest_approach_distance"], "derived": ["drv.motion.left_turn"], "justification": "'the vehicle making the left turn' is the same road user c3 binds: a road user of the admitted aggregate ru.aggregate=DEF-NRS-484A-320::vehicle, claimed as one atom, for which drv.motion.left_turn holds while it occupies the junction (rel.occupies on a region of kind st.intersection). 'shall yield the right-of-way' is DEF-NRS-484A-210's right 'to proceed in a lawful manner in preference to another vehicle ... unless one grants precedence to the other': the subject grants precedence by not coming into contact with that vehicle (rel.contact) and by not letting its closest approach to it fall below the clearance, which prim.closest_approach_within and prim.closest_approach_distance give under constant velocities within the horizon and rel.surface_gap measures between the nearest points of the bodies, with kin.speed the subject's own speed. rel.contact is not a stand-in for a near miss, which is why the primitives stand beside it."}], "operationalizations": [], "assumptions": [], "intentions": [], "compositions": [{"span": "c1", "rule": "NRS_484B_253_o1", "map": {"v": "t"}, "as": "compliance"}], "residues": [], "binders": [{"name": "v", "class_elements": ["ru.aggregate=DEF-NRS-484A-320::vehicle"]}], "applicability": "There is a vehicle t of the aggregate within an intersection making a left turn there, which has complied with the duty of NRS_484B_253_o1 ('having so yielded') and has given a left indication, by indicator or by arm signal, at some observation in the window p.turn_signal_advance_window behind the recognition of its turn; and the subject vehicle occupies a carrier whose entrance end is that intersection and whose designated direction is opposed to the direction of t's approach carrier.", "obligation": "At every such observation the subjec