way' is DEF-NRS-484A-210's right 'to proceed in a lawful manner in preference to another vehicle ... approaching under such circumstances of direction, speed and proximity as to give rise to the danger of a crash unless one grants precedence to the other': the subject grants precedence by not entering the junction at an observation at which the right-hand vehicle lies within it (drv.motion.region_entry on the subject, rel.occupies on the other, on the region of kind st.intersection the trigger binds), by not coming into contact with it (rel.contact, 'the bodies of two road users ... touch or overlap'), and by keeping clear of it while both are within the junction, which rel.surface_gap ('distance between the nearest points of two bodies, each body's footprint read with its own heading and extent'), prim.closest_approach_within and prim.closest_approach_distance measure under constant velocities within the horizon, with kin.speed the subject's own speed. rel.surface_gap is not read as an order of arrival -- the order is already settled by the two entries the trigger reads -- and rel.contact is not a stand-in for a near miss, which is why the closest-approach primitives stand beside it."}, {"span": "e1", "atoms": ["dev.governs", "st.intersection", "dev.traffic_signal", "dev.stop_sign", "dev.yield_sign", "dev.regulatory_sign", "dev.zone_sign", "dev.speed_limit_sign", "dev.lane_control_signal", "dev.pedestrian_signal", "dev.crossing_warning_signal", "dev.railway_signal_or_gate", "dev.temporary_traffic_control", "st.lane_marking", "st.centre_line", "rel.occupies", "st.travel_region", "st.lane_enters"], "derived": [], "justification": "The same words as in subsection 1 take the same atoms. 'official traffic-control devices' is DEF-NRS-484A-145, 'every sign, signal, marking and device ... placed or erected by a public authority or railroad for the purpose of regulating, warning or guiding traffic': the signals by dev.traffic_signal ('a signal head'), dev.lane_control_signal, dev.pedestrian_signal, dev.crossing_warning_signal and dev.railway_signal_or_gate; the signs by dev.stop_sign ('regulatory sign requiring a full halt'), dev.yield_sign, dev.regulatory_sign, dev.zone_sign and dev.speed_limit_sign; the markings by st.lane_marking and st.centre_line ('the marking, or the geometric centre, dividing the two directions of a two-way roadway'); the temporary devices by dev.temporary_traffic_control. 'at intersections controlled by' is dev.governs, 'the travel regions whose traffic the device controls ... or an intersection, read as control of the junction itself', read on the junction the two vehicles enter or on the subject's own approach carrier, which rel.occupies, st.travel_region and st.lane_enters bind."}, {"span": "e2", "atoms": ["ru.aggregate=DEF-NRS-484A-320::vehicle", "rel.occupies", "st.travel_region", "st.lane_enters", "st.lane_direction", "st.intersection"], "derived": [], "justification": "'vehicles approaching each other from opposite directions' is read as the ontology directs: rel.oncoming is 'not a stand-in for the direction a road user approaches from -- that is read through the carrier it approaches through, any carrier st.lane_enters admits, whose entrance end is the intersection, and through that carrier's direction (st.lane_direction) at the same instant'. Each vehicle occupies (rel.occupies) a carrier of kind st.travel_region whose entrance end is the same st.intersection (st.lane_enters), and the two carriers' designated directions are opposed: their normalised dot product is at or below the negative of p.same_direction_cosine_tolerance. The classes are the admitted aggregate ru.aggregate=DEF-NRS-484A-320::vehicle, claimed as one atom."}, {"span": "e4", "atoms": [], "derived": ["drv.motion.left_turn"], "justification": "'is making a left turn' is drv.motion.left_turn, 'the road user has turned to the left: counting from the onset of the turning ... the heading change accumulated since that onset reaches at least 