ntry_window of each other; the other vehicle bears to the subject's right in the subject's frame, so that the subject is the vehicle on the left. The duty does not apply where an official traffic-control device governs that junction or the subject's approach carrier -- unless either node of subsection 4 is engaged for the subject at that junction, which suspends that exception -- and it does not apply where the two carriers' designated directions are opposed and either vehicle is declared to intend a left turn at that junction or is making one.", "obligation": "From the entries on, the subject must grant precedence to the vehicle on its right: it must not enter the junction at an observation at which that vehicle lies within it, must not come into contact with it, and must not let its closest approach to it under constant velocities within p.yield_conflict_horizon fall below p.yield_min_clearance while that vehicle is within the junction.", "params": ["p.simultaneous_entry_window", "p.same_direction_cosine_tolerance", "p.heading_since_step_carla_scene_graph", "p.turn_onset_yaw_rate", "p.left_turn_angle", "p.yield_conflict_horizon", "p.yield_min_clearance"], "narrowings": [{"span": "ob1", "why": "'shall yield the right-of-way' is read as granting precedence in the three observable ways the definition's 'danger of a crash unless one grants precedence' admits on a trace: no entry while the right-hand vehicle lies within the junction, no contact, and no closest approach within the horizon closer than the clearance. Where both vehicles are already within the junction the first of the three is spent and the other two carry the duty.", "kind": "reading"}, {"span": "s1", "why": "'the driver of the vehicle on the left' is read through the vehicle's controlled motion: who or what is at the controls is not observable, and the duty binds that vehicle's conduct.", "kind": "observable_reading", "category": "agency"}, {"span": "e1", "why": "'official' is read as the presence of th