way' is DEF-NRS-484A-210's right 'to proceed in a lawful manner in preference to another vehicle ... approaching under such circumstances of direction, speed and proximity as to give rise to the danger of a crash unless one grants precedence to the other': the subject grants precedence by not entering the junction at an observation at which the right-hand vehicle lies within it (drv.motion.region_entry on the subject, rel.occupies on the other, on the region of kind st.intersection the trigger binds), by not coming into contact with it (rel.contact, 'the bodies of two road users ... touch or overlap'), and by keeping clear of it while both are within the junction, which rel.surface_gap ('distance between the nearest points of two bodies, each body's footprint read with its own heading and extent'), prim.closest_approach_within and prim.closest_approach_distance measure under constant velocities within the horizon, with kin.speed the subject's own speed. rel.surface_gap is not read as an order of arrival -- the order is already settled by the two entries the trigger reads -- and rel.contact is not a stand-in for a near miss, which is why the closest-approach primitives stand beside it."}, {"span": "e1", "atoms": ["dev.governs", "st.intersection", "dev.traffic_signal", "dev.stop_sign", "dev.yield_sign", "dev.regulatory_sign", "dev.zone_sign", "dev.speed_limit_sign", "dev.lane_control_signal", "dev.pedestrian_signal", "dev.crossing_warning_signal", "dev.railway_signal_or_gate", "dev.temporary_traffic_control", "st.lane_marking", "st.centre_line", "rel.occupies", "st.travel_region", "st.lane_enters"], "derived": [], "justification": "The same words as in subsection 1 take the same atoms. 'official traffic-control devices' is DEF-NRS-484A-145, 'every sign, signal, marking and device ... placed or erected by a public authority or railroad for the purpose of regulating, warning or guiding traffic': the signals by dev.traffic_signal ('a signal head'), dev.lane_control_signal, dev.pedestrian_signal, dev.crossing_warning_signal and dev.railway_signal_or_gate; the signs by dev.stop_sign ('regulatory sign requiring a full halt'), dev.yield_sign, dev.regulatory_sign, dev.zone_sign and dev.speed_limit_sign; the markings by st.lane_marking and st.centre_line ('the marking, or the geometric centre, dividing the two directions of a two-way roadway'); the temporary devices by dev.temporary_traffic_control. 'at intersections controlled by' is dev.governs, 'the travel regions whose traffic the device controls ... or an intersection, read as control of the junction itself', read on the junction the two vehicles enter or on the subject's own approach carrier, which rel.occupies, st.travel_region and st.lane_enters bind."}, {"span": "e2", "atoms": ["ru.aggregate=DEF-NRS-484A-320::vehicle", "rel.occupies", "st.travel_region", "st.lane_enters", "st.lane_direction", "st.intersection"], "derived": [], "justification": "'vehicles approaching each other from opposite directions' is read as the ontology directs: rel.oncoming is 'not a stand-in for the direction a road user approaches from -- that is read through the carrier it approaches through, any carrier st.lane_enters admits, whose entrance end is the intersection, and through that carrier's direction (st.lane_direction) at the same instant'. Each vehicle occupies (rel.occupies) a carrier of kind st.travel_region whose entrance end is the same st.intersection (st.lane_enters), and the two carriers' designated directions are opposed: their normalised dot product is at or below the negative of p.same_direction_cosine_tolerance. The classes are the admitted aggregate ru.aggregate=DEF-NRS-484A-320::vehicle, claimed as one atom."}, {"span": "e4", "atoms": [], "derived": ["drv.motion.left_turn"], "justification": "'is making a left turn' is drv.motion.left_turn, 'the road user has turned to the left: counting from the onset of the turning ... the heading change accumulated since that onset reaches at least the turn angle ... to the left', read on either of the two vehicles as 'one of the vehicles' allows. The concept states the turning of the body only; no signal and no declared intention stands in for it, and the intention the same words also name is carried separately."}], "operationalizations": [{"span": "st1", "standard": "at approximately the same time", "concepts": ["drv.motion.region_entry", "kin.time", "rel.occupies", "st.intersection"], "params": ["p.simultaneous_entry_window"], "convention": "Arrival-simultaneity convention: the two entries count as at approximately the same time where the interval between the observations at which each vehicle's footprint first comes to overlap the junction -- each read from kin.time, 'the instant of observation of a scene' -- is at most p.simultaneous_entry_window. The window is the headway within which two vehicles entering a junction from crossing highways are still both inside the junction's conflict area at ordinary approach speeds, so the closer the two entries the more surely the words hold and the farther apart the more surely they do not; it is the gap-acceptance figure for a crossing manoeuvre and not a figure of how much deference is enough.", "surrogate": false}], "assumptions": [], "intentions": [{"span": "e3", "id": "int.left_turn", "meaning": "the source's current plan for the road user is that it turn to the left at the region named as the declaration's target"}], "compositions": [{"span": "r1", "rule": "NRS_484B_250_4_o1", "map": {"v": "v"}, "as": "unless", "scopes": "e1"}, {"span": "r1", "rule": "NRS_484B_250_4_o2", "map": {"v": "v"}, "as": "unless", "scopes": "e1"}], "residues": [], "binders": [{"name": "v", "class_elements": ["ru.aggregate=DEF-NRS-484A-320::vehicle"]}], "applicability": "The subject vehicle and another vehicle of the aggregate each enter one and the same intersection, each from a carrier lying on a highway other than the other's, and the two entry observations lie within p.simultaneous_entry_window of each other; the other vehicle bears to the subject's right in the subject's frame, so that the subject is the vehicle on the left. The duty does not apply where an official traffic-control device governs that junction or the subject's approach carrier -- unless either node of subsection 4 is engaged for the subject at that junction, which suspends that exception -- and it does not apply where the two carriers' designated directions are opposed and either vehicle is declared to intend a left turn at that junction or is making one.", "obligation": "From the entries on, the subject must grant precedence to the vehicle on its right: it must not enter the junction at an observation at which that vehicle lies within it, must not come into contact with it, and must not let its closest approach to it under constant velocities within p.yield_conflict_horizon fall below p.yield_min_clearance while that vehicle is within the junction.", "params": ["p.simultaneous_entry_window", "p.same_direction_cosine_tolerance", "p.heading_since_step_carla_scene_graph", "p.turn_onset_yaw_rate", "p.left_turn_angle", "p.yield_conflict_horizon", "p.yield_min_clearance"], "narrowings": [{"span": "ob1", "why": "'shall yield the right-of-way' is read as granting precedence in the three observable ways the definition's 'danger of a crash unless one grants precedence' admits on a trace: no entry while the right-hand vehicle lies within the junction, no contact, and no closest approach within the horizon closer than the clearance. Where both vehicles are already within the junction the first of the three is spent and the other two carry the duty.", "kind": "reading"}, {"span": "s1", "why": "'the driver of the vehicle on the left' is read through the vehicle's controlled motion: who or what is at the controls is not observable, and the duty binds that vehicle's conduct.", "kind": "observable_reading", "category": "agency"}, {"span": "e1", "why": "'official' is read as the presence of th